📢 <b>Data Layer Event</b>
<br>
Push a predefined event to the data layer when consent state is modified by this template. Alternatively, specify a custom event name that better suits the needs of your specific setup.
<br><br>
<b>Pre-defined event names:</b><br>
🔹 consent_default<br>
🔹 consent_update
<br><br>
<b>Example event:</b><br>
dataLayer.push({<br>
&emsp;
event: "<b>consent_&lt;command></b>",<br>
&emsp;
<b>consent_state</b>: {<br>
&emsp;&emsp;
analytics_storage,<br>
&emsp;&emsp;
ad_storage,<br>
&emsp;&emsp;
ad_user_data,<br>
&emsp;&emsp;
ad_personalization,<br>
&emsp;&emsp;
personalization_storage,<br>
&emsp;&emsp;
functionality_storage,<br>
&emsp;&emsp;
security_storage<br>
&emsp;
},<br>
&emsp;
<em>consent_state_previous</em> (optional, see <b>Include Previous State</b>)<br>
})
<br><br>
<b>consent_state</b> holds every consent type this template has set on the current page, with the latest command merged over the earlier ones. Consent types that have not been set are left out, and so are <em>region</em> and <em>wait_for_update</em>.

⚙️ <b>Include Previous Consent State</b>
<br>
Includes the additional variable <b>consent_state_previous</b> in the data layer event that is pushed together with the <b>update</b> command. The variable holds the consent state that was last set by this template on the current page, and is undefined on the first fire after a page load.
<br><br>
<b>Example event:</b><br>
dataLayer.push({<br>
&emsp;
event: "<b>consent_update</b>",<br>
&emsp;
consent_state, (current consent state)<br>
&emsp;
<b>consent_state_previous</b>: {<br>
&emsp;&emsp;
analytics_storage,<br>
&emsp;&emsp;
ad_storage,<br>
&emsp;&emsp;
ad_user_data,<br>
&emsp;&emsp;
ad_personalization,<br>
&emsp;&emsp;
personalization_storage,<br>
&emsp;&emsp;
functionality_storage,<br>
&emsp;&emsp;
security_storage<br>
&emsp;
}<br>
})
